meta {
  name: Login (via oms-main)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{authBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "Admin@123"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.accessToken) {
    console.log("🚀 Script executed successfully!");
    bru.setEnvVar("token", res.body.accessToken);
    console.log("Token: " + bru.getEnvVar("token"));
  }
}

docs {
  product-service does not issue tokens itself — it only verifies them (see
  security.SecurityConfig, which validates against oms-main's JWKS endpoint,
  not a login flow of its own). This request hits oms-main's real login
  endpoint (authBaseUrl, a separate env var from this collection's own
  baseUrl) purely to obtain a token, then stores it in this collection's own
  `token` env var — every product request below sends it automatically as
  its Bearer token, same as oms-main's own collection does.

  Default credentials are the admin account oms-main bootstraps automatically
  on first startup (see that repo's application.properties:
  app.security.default-admin-username / app.security.default-admin-password).

  If authBaseUrl doesn't point at a reachable oms-main instance, this request
  (and therefore every authenticated request below) will fail — product-service
  being reachable is not enough on its own.
}
